{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE INTEGRITY CENTRE — ONE CITABLE DOCUMENT
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  This page was a summary with doors: ten short sections, each a card, each with a
  link out to the Help Centre. That shape was right when the page's only job was to
  answer "how is a winner decided" in a minute.

  It has a second job now. The philosophy behind community voting is a POSITION —
  the sort of thing a journalist quotes, a regulator asks for, and a nominee's
  lawyer reads twice — and positions have to be citable. A card grid cannot be
  cited. So the page is now built as an article: one column, continuous numbering,
  a stated version and date, and Copy / Download / Cite in the header.

  ── EDITORIAL, NOT DECORATIVE ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  The styling below is deliberately plainer than the rest of the site. No cards, no
  gradients, no shadows, no progress bars. Warm paper, one measure of about 66
  characters, Playfair for headings and DM Sans for body at a generous 1.78 leading,
  and hairline rules doing all the separating that panels used to do.

  Data that used to be a bar chart is now a table, because a table can be read
  aloud, copied into a spreadsheet, and printed — and every one of those matters
  more for this document than the bar did.

  ── WHERE THE WORDS LIVE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Part I is NOT written here. It arrives as `doc_sections` from
  {@see \AfricaGates\Services\CommunityVotingPhilosophy}, because the same prose has
  to leave as HTML, as the .txt the Copy button lifts, and as the .md the Download
  button saves. One source, three surfaces, no drift.

  Part II is written here, and every figure in it is a route variable read from
  RuleEngine — the same object the scorer consults. Of every page on this site the
  methodology page is the one that must not go on describing a system the code has
  stopped running.
#}

{% set part2_offset = doc_sections|default([])|length %}

{#
  ── STRUCTURED DATA & CITATION METADATA ─────────────────────────────────────

  Three things, for three different readers:

  1. `Article` — tells a search engine this is a dated, versioned document with an
     author and a publisher, which is what earns the byline treatment in results.
  2. Highwire Press `citation_*` tags plus Dublin Core — what Zotero, Mendeley and
     Google Scholar actually read when somebody clicks "save citation". Without
     them a reference manager guesses the title from the <title> tag and the date
     from nothing.
  3. `FAQPage` — kept from the previous build, and still built only from questions
     this page VISIBLY answers. Marking up an answer a reader cannot find is the
     thing search engines penalise, and it is also just a lie in a format nobody
     reads.
#}
{% block structured_data %}
<meta name="citation_title" content="{{ doc_title }}">
<meta name="citation_author" content="{{ doc_author }}">
<meta name="citation_publisher" content="{{ doc_publisher }}">
<meta name="citation_publication_date" content="{{ doc_published }}">
<meta name="citation_online_date" content="{{ doc_updated }}">
<meta name="citation_public_url" content="{{ doc_url }}">
<meta name="DC.title" content="{{ doc_title }}">
<meta name="DC.creator" content="{{ doc_author }}">
<meta name="DC.publisher" content="{{ doc_publisher }}">
<meta name="DC.date" content="{{ doc_updated }}">
<meta name="DC.identifier" content="{{ doc_url }}">
<meta name="DC.type" content="Text">
<meta name="DC.format" content="text/html">
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" type="application/ld+json">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article",
"headline":{{ doc_title|json_encode|raw }},
"alternativeHeadline":{{ doc_subtitle|json_encode|raw }},
"description":{{ doc_standfirst|striptags|json_encode|raw }},
"author":{"@type":"Organization","name":{{ doc_author|json_encode|raw }}},
"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":{{ doc_publisher|json_encode|raw }}},
"datePublished":{{ doc_published|json_encode|raw }},
"dateModified":{{ doc_updated|json_encode|raw }},
"version":{{ doc_version|json_encode|raw }},
"inLanguage":"en",
"isAccessibleForFree":true,
"license":{{ (_site_url ~ '/terms')|json_encode|raw }},
"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":{{ doc_url|json_encode|raw }}},
"url":{{ doc_url|json_encode|raw }}}
</script>
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" type="application/ld+json">
{% set faq = [
  {
    q: 'How is the Cultural Power Index calculated?',
    a: 'The CPI is ' ~ community_pct|default(45) ~ '% verified community votes and ' ~ judge_pct|default(55) ~ '% independent judge panel. The community share is normalised within each category, so a nominee in a small category is measured against their own field rather than against the whole platform.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is voting on Africa GATES paid?',
    a: 'A token contribution gives a supporter a practical way of standing with a nominee, and it funds the judging, verification and production work behind the programme. It is not a purchase of an award: contributions add to a public tally but are held in a column the scorer never reads.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you buy votes to win an Africa GATES award?',
    a: 'No. Contributions add to a nominee’s public tally but are held in a separate column the scorer never reads, they cannot break a tie, and they are capped at ' ~ paid_cap_pct|default(50) ~ '% of the organic support a nominee has earned. Money can make a nominee look more popular; it cannot make them win.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is the public vote only ' ~ community_pct|default(45) ~ '%?',
    a: 'Because popularity is not the same thing as excellence. A larger following is not greater impact, and a nominee with more capacity to mobilise supporters is not necessarily the strongest candidate. Limiting the public vote to ' ~ community_pct|default(45) ~ '% leaves ' ~ judge_pct|default(55) ~ '% for structured, independent assessment.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Why might the nominee with the most votes not win?',
    a: 'Winning also requires at least ' ~ min_judges|default(2) ~ ' complete judge scorecards. A partial scorecard counts as nothing, judges recuse themselves from nominees they are connected to, and if nobody in a category reaches the quorum the award is not given.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if two nominees tie?',
    a: 'The tiebreak is organic votes — the free, code-verified ones. Contributions are not consulted, so the closest possible race is decided by people rather than by spending. A tie on both the index and organic votes is recorded as a dead heat and escalated to the integrity team.'
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you know the results were not edited afterwards?',
    a: 'Every computed standing is sealed with a fingerprint of itself and of the record before it, so editing an old result breaks every record after it. The chain is re-verified automatically every day, and the database refuses to record two standings claiming the same predecessor.'
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the Africa GATES community return?',
    a: 'A nominee keeps ' ~ return_pct|default('50') ~ '% of what supporters contribute in their name, win or lose, once they have gathered ' ~ return_threshold|default(250) ~ ' votes of qualifying support. No single supporter can supply more than ' ~ return_cap_pct|default(10) ~ '% of that threshold, so qualifying takes at least ' ~ return_people|default(10) ~ ' different verified people.'
  },
  {
    q: 'Is Africa GATES a pyramid or Ponzi scheme?',
    a: 'No. Africa GATES is not a Ponzi scheme, pyramid scheme, MLM programme, investment scheme or get-rich-quick scheme. Nobody is promised a financial return for recruiting other participants, and no participant earns money by introducing another person into the programme.'
  }
] %}
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{% for f in faq %}{"@type":"Question","name":{{ f.q|json_encode|raw }},"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":{{ f.a|json_encode|raw }}}}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}]}
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  /* ══ THE PAPER ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     A warm sheet rather than the site's cool white. The document is meant to
     feel like something printed and kept, and #fbfbfa reads as a screen.

     The tokens are declared on BODY, not on .ar. Custom properties inherit
     downward only, so a --ar-paper defined on .ar is invisible to the body
     element that has to paint the background — which is exactly how this
     shipped white the first time. Declaring them here puts both the painter
     and its descendants inside the same scope. */
  body[data-page="integrity"]{
    --ar-paper:#f4f2ea;
    --ar-ink:#12292b;
    --ar-soft:#5b6663;          /* ≥4.5:1 on the paper — body-adjacent text */
    --ar-faint:#7c8683;         /* ≥3:1 — labels and furniture only, never prose */
    --ar-line:rgba(18,41,43,.14);
    --ar-line-soft:rgba(18,41,43,.08);
    --ar-accent:#237b22;
    --ar-accent-dark:#1a6118;
    --ar-gold:#9a7726;
    --ar-measure:42rem;         /* ≈66 characters at the body size */
    background:var(--ar-paper);
    color:var(--ar-ink);
  }

  /* ══ SHELL ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     One column of prose, with the contents parked in the margin from 1180px up.
     Below that the rail becomes an inline block at the top, because a sticky
     sidebar on a narrow screen is a sticky obstruction. */
  .ar-shell{ max-width:74rem; margin:0 auto; padding:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.4rem) var(--ag-gutter,32px) clamp(4rem,8vw,6rem); }
  @media (min-width:1180px){
    .ar-shell{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 15rem; gap:4rem; align-items:start; }
    .ar-rail{ position:sticky; top:calc(var(--ag-nav-h,72px) + 1.5rem); order:2; }
    .ar-body{ order:1; }
  }
  .ar-body{ max-width:var(--ar-measure); }

  /* ══ TYPE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-body p, .ar-body li{ font-family:var(--ag-font-body); font-size:17.5px; line-height:1.78; color:var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-body p{ margin:0 0 1.35em; }
  .ar-body a{ color:var(--ar-accent-dark); text-decoration:underline; text-decoration-thickness:1px; text-underline-offset:.16em; }
  .ar-body a:hover{ text-decoration-thickness:2px; }
  .ar-body code{ font-family:var(--ag-font-mono); font-size:.9em; background:rgba(18,41,43,.06); padding:.12em .38em; border-radius:4px; }

  /* ══ MASTHEAD ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-eyebrow{ margin:0 0 1.1rem; font:600 11px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-accent); }
  .ar-h1{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:clamp(2.15rem,5.2vw,3.35rem); line-height:1.07; letter-spacing:-.022em; color:var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-sub{ margin:.85rem 0 0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-style:italic; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.6vw,1.42rem); line-height:1.4; color:var(--ar-soft); }
  .ar-stand{ margin:1.7rem 0 0; font-size:19px !important; line-height:1.72 !important; color:var(--ar-soft) !important; }

  /* The byline row. Hairline above and below, mono, small — a colophon, not a
     headline. Wraps to two lines on a phone without becoming a list. */
  .ar-meta{ margin:2rem 0 0; padding:.9rem 0; border-top:1px solid var(--ar-line); border-bottom:1px solid var(--ar-line);
            display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.4rem 1.4rem; font:500 12px/1.5 var(--ag-font-mono); color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-meta b{ color:var(--ar-soft); font-weight:600; }
  .ar-meta dfn{ font-style:normal; }

  /* ══ TOOLBAR ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Copy, Download, Cite. Hairline and quiet: these are utilities on a
     document, not calls to action, and styling them as buttons would make them
     compete with the words. */
  .ar-tools{ margin:1.5rem 0 0; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.55rem; position:relative; }
  .ar-tool{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem; cursor:pointer; background:transparent;
            border:1px solid var(--ar-line); border-radius:999px; padding:.5rem .95rem;
            font:600 12.5px/1 var(--ag-font-body); color:var(--ar-ink); text-decoration:none;
            transition:border-color .15s, background-color .15s; }
  .ar-tool:hover{ border-color:var(--ar-accent); background:rgba(35,123,34,.05); text-decoration:none; }
  .ar-tool[aria-expanded="true"]{ border-color:var(--ar-accent); background:rgba(35,123,34,.06); }
  .ar-tool.is-done{ border-color:var(--ar-accent); color:var(--ar-accent-dark); background:rgba(35,123,34,.08); }
  .ar-tool svg{ flex:none; }

  /* The download menu. A popover rather than two more buttons in the row,
     because .md and .txt are one decision with two answers. */
  .ar-pop{ position:absolute; top:calc(100% + .45rem); left:0; z-index:20; min-width:15rem;
           background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--ar-line); border-radius:12px; padding:.35rem;
           box-shadow:0 12px 32px -12px rgba(18,41,43,.28); }
  .ar-pop a{ display:block; padding:.6rem .7rem; border-radius:8px; text-decoration:none; color:var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-pop a:hover{ background:rgba(18,41,43,.05); text-decoration:none; }
  .ar-pop b{ display:block; font:600 13.5px/1.3 var(--ag-font-body); }
  .ar-pop span{ display:block; margin-top:2px; font-size:12px; line-height:1.45; color:var(--ar-faint); }

  /* Announced to screen readers, shown to everybody. One line, no layout shift. */
  .ar-say{ margin:.7rem 0 0; min-height:1.1rem; font:500 12.5px/1.1 var(--ag-font-mono); color:var(--ar-accent-dark); }

  /* ══ CONTENTS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-rail h2, .ar-toc h2{ margin:0 0 .8rem; font:600 11px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-rail ol, .ar-toc ol{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; counter-reset:ar; }
  .ar-rail li, .ar-toc li{ counter-increment:ar; }
  .ar-rail a, .ar-toc a{ display:flex; gap:.6rem; padding:.32rem 0; font-size:13.5px !important; line-height:1.45 !important;
                         color:var(--ar-soft) !important; text-decoration:none; }
  .ar-rail a::before, .ar-toc a::before{ content:counter(ar,decimal-leading-zero); flex:none; font:600 10.5px/1.7 var(--ag-font-mono); color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-rail a:hover, .ar-toc a:hover{ color:var(--ar-accent-dark) !important; text-decoration:none; }
  .ar-rail .ar-part, .ar-toc .ar-part{ margin:1rem 0 .35rem; font:600 10.5px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-accent); }
  .ar-rail .ar-part:first-child, .ar-toc .ar-part:first-child{ margin-top:0; }
  /* The part labels and the reference entry are <li> because they live inside the
     <ol> — but they are not sections, so they must not consume a number. Without
     this the contents counted them and every entry was off by one per part: the
     body said "13 The score" while the contents said 15. */
  .ar-rail li.ar-part, .ar-toc li.ar-part,
  .ar-rail li.ar-ref, .ar-toc li.ar-ref{ counter-increment:none; }
  .ar-rail li.ar-ref a::before, .ar-toc li.ar-ref a::before{ content:"§"; }
  /* Inline contents, for the narrow layout only. */
  .ar-toc{ margin:2.6rem 0 0; padding:1.2rem 1.3rem; border:1px solid var(--ar-line); border-radius:14px; }
  @media (min-width:1180px){ .ar-toc{ display:none; } }
  .ar-rail{ display:none; }
  @media (min-width:1180px){ .ar-rail{ display:block; } }

  /* ══ PART DIVIDER ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-part-head{ margin:clamp(3.4rem,7vw,5rem) 0 0; padding-top:1.6rem; border-top:2px solid var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-part-head .ar-pn{ display:block; font:600 11px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-accent); margin-bottom:.7rem; }
  .ar-part-head h2{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3.6vw,2.2rem); line-height:1.15; letter-spacing:-.018em; }
  .ar-part-head p{ margin:.75rem 0 0; color:var(--ar-soft) !important; }

  /* ══ SECTIONS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-sec{ scroll-margin-top:calc(var(--ag-nav-h,72px) + 1.5rem); margin-top:clamp(2.6rem,5.5vw,3.6rem); }
  .ar-sec > h3{ margin:0 0 1.1rem; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700;
                font-size:clamp(1.42rem,3vw,1.78rem); line-height:1.22; letter-spacing:-.016em; color:var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-sn{ display:block; margin-bottom:.5rem; font:600 11px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.16em; color:var(--ar-accent); }
  .ar-h4{ margin:2rem 0 .7rem; font-family:var(--ag-font-body); font-weight:700; font-size:1.02rem; line-height:1.4;
          letter-spacing:.01em; color:var(--ar-ink); }

  /* ══ LISTS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     Hanging markers, so the text block keeps one left edge with the paragraphs
     around it. A bullet that pushes prose inward breaks the column. */
  .ar-list{ list-style:none; margin:0 0 1.35em; padding:0; }
  .ar-list li{ position:relative; padding-left:1.35rem; margin-bottom:.6em; }
  .ar-list li::before{ content:""; position:absolute; left:.25rem; top:.72em; width:5px; height:5px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--ar-accent); }
  .ar-steps{ list-style:none; margin:0 0 1.35em; padding:0; counter-reset:st; }
  .ar-steps li{ position:relative; padding-left:2.1rem; margin-bottom:.7em; counter-increment:st; }
  .ar-steps li::before{ content:counter(st,decimal-leading-zero); position:absolute; left:0; top:.28em;
                        font:600 11.5px/1.6 var(--ag-font-mono); color:var(--ar-accent); }

  /* ══ PULL QUOTE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     The document's own voice. Playfair italic, no quotation marks — the marks
     are what make a pull quote look like a testimonial. */
  .ar-quote{ margin:2.1rem 0; padding:0 0 0 1.5rem; border-left:2px solid var(--ar-accent); }
  .ar-quote p{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-style:italic; font-weight:400;
               font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.6vw,1.44rem) !important; line-height:1.48 !important; color:var(--ar-ink) !important; }

  /* ══ TABLE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     What used to be bar charts. Hairline rows, mono figures, and a scroll
     container so a narrow screen scrolls the table instead of the page. */
  .ar-tw{ margin:0 0 1.5em; overflow-x:auto; }
  .ar-table{ width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; font-family:var(--ag-font-body); }
  .ar-table caption{ caption-side:top; text-align:left; margin-bottom:.7rem;
                     font:600 11px/1.4 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-table th, .ar-table td{ text-align:left; padding:.72rem .9rem .72rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--ar-line-soft);
                              font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.6; vertical-align:baseline; }
  .ar-table thead th{ border-bottom:1px solid var(--ar-line); font-weight:600; font-size:12.5px;
                      letter-spacing:.04em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-table tbody th{ font-weight:600; color:var(--ar-ink); white-space:nowrap; }
  .ar-table td:last-child, .ar-table th:last-child{ padding-right:0; }
  .ar-table .ar-num{ font-family:var(--ag-font-mono); font-weight:600; font-size:14.5px; color:var(--ar-accent-dark); white-space:nowrap; }
  .ar-table tfoot td{ border-bottom:0; padding-top:.9rem; font-size:14px; color:var(--ar-soft); }

  /* ══ TWO COLUMNS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     "What it does" against "what it does not". A single hairline between them
     carries the contrast; the previous build used a green panel and a red one,
     which read as a warning rather than as a distinction. */
  .ar-cols{ margin:0 0 1.5em; display:grid; gap:1.6rem; }
  @media (min-width:640px){ .ar-cols{ grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:2.2rem; } }
  .ar-cols > div + div{ padding-top:1.6rem; border-top:1px solid var(--ar-line); }
  @media (min-width:640px){
    .ar-cols > div + div{ padding-top:0; border-top:0; padding-left:2.2rem; border-left:1px solid var(--ar-line); }
  }
  .ar-cols h4{ margin:0 0 .8rem; font:600 12px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.13em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .ar-cols--can h4{ color:var(--ar-accent-dark); }
  .ar-cols--cannot h4{ color:#a2453f; }
  .ar-cols li{ font-size:16px !important; line-height:1.7 !important; }
  .ar-cols .ar-list li::before{ background:currentColor; opacity:.5; }
  .ar-cols--cannot .ar-list li::before{ background:#a2453f; }

  /* ══ NOTICE ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     One on the page: the anti-fraud disclaimer. Being the only boxed thing in
     the document is what makes the box mean something. */
  .ar-note{ margin:1.6rem 0 1.5em; padding:1.4rem 1.5rem; background:rgba(154,119,38,.07);
            border:1px solid rgba(154,119,38,.28); border-radius:14px; }
  .ar-note h4{ margin:0 0 .9rem; font:600 11.5px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.15em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-gold); }
  .ar-note p{ font-size:16px !important; line-height:1.72 !important; }
  .ar-note p:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }

  /* ══ ASIDE / FOOTNOTE ════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-aside{ margin:1.5rem 0; padding-left:1.2rem; border-left:1px solid var(--ar-line); }
  .ar-aside p{ margin:0; font-size:15.5px !important; line-height:1.7 !important; color:var(--ar-soft) !important; }

  /* Further reading — a line of references, the way an article ends a section. */
  .ar-refs{ margin:1.4rem 0 0; padding-top:.9rem; border-top:1px solid var(--ar-line-soft); }
  .ar-refs span{ font:600 10.5px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ar-faint); }
  .ar-refs ul{ list-style:none; margin:.6rem 0 0; padding:0; }
  .ar-refs li{ margin-bottom:.3rem; font-size:14.5px !important; line-height:1.6 !important; }
  .ar-refs a{ color:var(--ar-soft) !important; text-decoration-color:var(--ar-line); }
  .ar-refs a:hover{ color:var(--ar-accent-dark) !important; }

  /* ══ CITATION ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-cite{ scroll-margin-top:calc(var(--ag-nav-h,72px) + 1.5rem); margin:clamp(3.4rem,7vw,5rem) 0 0; padding-top:1.6rem; border-top:2px solid var(--ar-ink); }
  .ar-cite > h2{ margin:0 0 .5rem; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3.2vw,1.9rem); letter-spacing:-.016em; }
  .ar-tabs{ margin:1.4rem 0 0; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.4rem; border-bottom:1px solid var(--ar-line); padding-bottom:.7rem; }
  .ar-tab{ cursor:pointer; background:transparent; border:1px solid transparent; border-radius:999px; padding:.4rem .8rem;
           font:600 12.5px/1 var(--ag-font-body); color:var(--ar-soft); }
  .ar-tab:hover{ color:var(--ar-ink); background:rgba(18,41,43,.05); }
  .ar-tab[aria-selected="true"]{ background:var(--ar-ink); color:#f4f2ea; }
  .ar-cite-body{ margin:1.1rem 0 0; }
  .ar-body .ar-cite-text{ margin:0; padding:1.1rem 1.2rem; background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--ar-line); border-radius:12px;
                 font-family:var(--ag-font-mono) !important; font-size:13.5px !important; line-height:1.75 !important; color:var(--ar-ink);
                 white-space:pre-wrap; word-break:break-word; }
  .ar-cite-act{ margin:.8rem 0 0; display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:.55rem; align-items:center; }

  /* ══ CLOSING ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ar-end{ margin:clamp(3rem,6vw,4rem) 0 0; padding-top:1.6rem; border-top:1px solid var(--ar-line); }
  .ar-end p{ color:var(--ar-soft) !important; font-size:16px !important; }

  /* ══ PRINT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     A document with a Download button will be printed, so it gets a print
     stylesheet rather than whatever the browser improvises. Utilities and the
     contents rail go; the URL and version stay, because a printed page that
     cannot be traced back to its source cannot be cited from either. */
  @media print{
    body[data-page="integrity"]{ background:#fff; }
    .ar-tools, .ar-rail, .ar-toc, .ar-say, .ar-tabs, .ar-cite-act{ display:none !important; }
    .ar-shell{ max-width:none; padding:0; display:block; }
    .ar-body{ max-width:none; }
    .ar-body p, .ar-body li{ font-size:11pt; line-height:1.55; }
    .ar-sec, .ar-part-head, .ar-cite{ break-inside:avoid-page; }
    .ar-sec > h3, .ar-part-head h2{ break-after:avoid-page; }
    .ar-note{ border:1px solid #999; background:none; }
    .ar-cite-text{ background:none; border:1px solid #999; }
    .ar-body a::after{ content:" (" attr(href) ")"; font-size:9pt; color:#555; word-break:break-all; }
    .ar-refs a::after{ content:""; }
  }
</style>
